   "date": "2022-06-30T21:04:38Z",
   "subject": "Re: [geomorph-r-package] Question about the appropriate model fit for comparing species among different clades",
   "parts": [
    [
     1,
     "<div dir=\"ltr\"><div class=\"gmail_default\" style=\"font-family:arial,sans-serif;font-size:small;color:#000000\">Hi Bryan, <br></div><div class=\"gmail_default\" style=\"font-family:arial,sans-serif;font-size:small;color:#000000\">Thanks for your early response. Sorry for the typo, it was an error adapting my original code to the email. I wanted to write: <br></div><div class=\"gmail_default\" style=\"font-family:arial,sans-serif;font-size:small;color:#000000\">fit_common &lt;- procD.lm(coords ~ log(Csize) + species</div><div class=\"gmail_default\" style=\"font-family:arial,sans-serif;font-size:small;color:#000000\"><br></div><div class=\"gmail_default\" style=\"font-family:arial,sans-serif;font-size:small;color:#000000\">Regarding your comment about the nested approach. Are the following codes correct to assess differences between species, nested into clades? <span class=\"gmail_default\" style=\"font-family:arial,sans-serif;font-size:small;color:rgb(0,0,0)\">Or the correct order should be species/clade ? <br></span></div><div class=\"gmail_default\" style=\"font-family:arial,sans-serif;font-size:small;color:#000000\"><span class=\"gmail_default\" style=\"font-family:arial,sans-serif;font-size:small;color:rgb(0,0,0)\"><br></span></div><div class=\"gmail_default\" style=\"font-family:arial,sans-serif;font-size:small;color:#000000\">fit_unique &lt;- procD.lm(coords ~ log(Csize)*clade/species, SS.type = &quot;III&quot;,</div></div>"
    ],
    [
     2,
     "<div dir=\"ltr\"><div class=\"gmail_default\" style=\"font-family:arial,sans-serif;font-size:small;color:#000000\"><br>                                data = gdf, print.progress = FALSE)<br> </div></div>"
    ],
    [
     1,
     "<div dir=\"ltr\"><div class=\"gmail_default\" style=\"font-family:arial,sans-serif;font-size:small;color:#000000\"></div><div class=\"gmail_default\" style=\"font-family:arial,sans-serif;font-size:small;color:#000000\">fit_common &lt;- procD.lm(coords ~ log(Csize) + clade/species, SS.type = &quot;III&quot;,</div></div>"
    ],
    [
     2,
     "<div dir=\"ltr\"><div class=\"gmail_default\" style=\"font-family:arial,sans-serif;font-size:small;color:#000000\"><br>                                data = gdf, print.progress = FALSE) </div></div>"
    ],
    [
     1,
     "<div dir=\"ltr\"><div class=\"gmail_default\" style=\"font-family:arial,sans-serif;font-size:small;color:#000000\"></div><div><span class=\"gmail_default\" style=\"font-family:arial,sans-serif;font-size:small;color:rgb(0,0,0)\">anova (fit_common, fit_unique)</span></div><div><span class=\"gmail_default\" style=\"font-family:arial,sans-serif;font-size:small;color:rgb(0,0,0)\"><br></span></div><div><span class=\"gmail_default\" style=\"font-family:arial,sans-serif;font-size:small;color:rgb(0,0,0)\"><br></span></div><div><span class=\"gmail_default\" style=\"font-family:arial,sans-serif;font-size:small;color:rgb(0,0,0)\">Best. Thanks in advance</span></div><div><span class=\"gmail_default\" style=\"font-family:arial,sans-serif;font-size:small;color:rgb(0,0,0)\"><br></span></div><div><span class=\"gmail_default\" style=\"font-family:arial,sans-serif;font-size:small;color:rgb(0,0,0)\">Julio<br></span></div></div>\r\n"
