   "parts": [
    [
     1,
     "<div dir=\"ltr\"><div class=\"gmail_default\" style=\"font-family:arial,helvetica,sans-serif;font-size:small\">Yes, &quot;clade/species&quot; is species nested within each clade. The following contains some discussion of nested model terms, which I have less experience with: <a href=\"https://cran.r-project.org/web/packages/RRPP/vignettes/Using.RRPP.html\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=https://cran.r-project.org/web/packages/RRPP/vignettes/Using.RRPP.html&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1792483843454000&amp;usg=AOvVaw39qo8WZkOWE61-ZY8hgq9e\">https://cran.r-project.org/web/packages/RRPP/vignettes/Using.RRPP.html</a>.</div><div class=\"gmail_default\" style=\"font-family:arial,helvetica,sans-serif;font-size:small\"><br></div><div class=\"gmail_default\" style=\"font-family:arial,helvetica,sans-serif;font-size:small\">Best,</div><div class=\"gmail_default\" style=\"font-family:arial,helvetica,sans-serif;font-size:small\">Bryan</div></div><br><div class=\"gmail_quote\"></div>"
    ],
    [
     3,
     "<div class=\"gmail_quote\"><div dir=\"ltr\" class=\"gmail_attr\">On Thu, Jun 30, 2022 at 2:04 PM Julio Torres &lt;<a href data-email-masked rel=\"nofollow\">juliomy...@gmail.com</a>&gt; wrote:<br></div></div>"
    ],
    [
     3,
     "<div class=\"gmail_quote\"><blockquote class=\"gmail_quote\" style=\"margin:0px 0px 0px 0.8ex;border-left:1px solid rgb(204,204,204);padding-left:1ex\"><div dir=\"ltr\"><div class=\"gmail_default\" style=\"font-family:arial,sans-serif;font-size:small;color:rgb(0,0,0)\">Hi Bryan, <br></div><div class=\"gmail_default\" style=\"font-family:arial,sans-serif;font-size:small;color:rgb(0,0,0)\">Thanks for your early response. Sorry for the typo, it was an error adapting my original code to the email. I wanted to write: <br></div><div class=\"gmail_default\" style=\"font-family:arial,sans-serif;font-size:small;color:rgb(0,0,0)\">fit_common &lt;- procD.lm(coords ~ log(Csize) + species</div><div class=\"gmail_default\" style=\"font-family:arial,sans-serif;font-size:small;color:rgb(0,0,0)\"><br></div><div class=\"gmail_default\" style=\"font-family:arial,sans-serif;font-size:small;color:rgb(0,0,0)\">Regarding your comment about the nested approach. Are the following codes correct to assess differences between species, nested into clades? <span class=\"gmail_default\" style=\"font-family:arial,sans-serif;font-size:small;color:rgb(0,0,0)\">Or the correct order should be species/clade ? <br></span></div><div class=\"gmail_default\" style=\"font-family:arial,sans-serif;font-size:small;color:rgb(0,0,0)\"><span class=\"gmail_default\" style=\"font-family:arial,sans-serif;font-size:small;color:rgb(0,0,0)\"><br></span></div><div class=\"gmail_default\" style=\"font-family:arial,sans-serif;font-size:small;color:rgb(0,0,0)\">fit_unique &lt;- procD.lm(coords ~ log(Csize)*clade/species, SS.type = &quot;III&quot;,<br>                                data = gdf, print.progress = FALSE)<br> </div><div class=\"gmail_default\" style=\"font-family:arial,sans-serif;font-size:small;color:rgb(0,0,0)\">fit_common &lt;- procD.lm(coords ~ log(Csize) + clade/species, SS.type = &quot;III&quot;,<br>                                data = gdf, print.progress = FALSE) </div><div><span class=\"gmail_de